WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:03.270
DECEMBER 21, 2021

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:02.850
Another error.

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.480
It's happening at the information sensor
at the system's core.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.610
Send me details of the errors immediately.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:13.030
I'll organize and prepare the information
and send it to Hazard Cast.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:17.030
<i>This amount can't be processed by a human.</i>

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:22.370
<i>Looking at the case, it's something that Asumi
wouldn't want to make a decision for.</i>

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:28.460
<i>And I'm definitely sure that Asumi's conscience
has awoken within the KANAE System.</i>

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.760
I'm going to save Asumi?

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:39.180
Does that mean I can return her
to the life she used to have?

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:46.520
I said this earlier, but Miss Asumi
is already dead biologically.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:51.480
The only choices you have are to eradicate
Miss Asumi from the system,

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.650
or to make her enter an eternal slumber
within the system.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.660
Which do you think will be her salvation?

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.740
Another trolley dilemma.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.580
There's no way I can choose.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:07.920
However, making the choice is the only way.

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:11.920
Excuse me.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:12.800
Chikuwa.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.050
Hey, Satchan.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.300
Sleeping Beauty has woken up.
I feel reassured.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.300
I'm sorry to have troubled you.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.680
Shuta.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.770
Excuse me a sec.

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:28.150
Shuta Aoi. You are under arrest
for suspicion of terrorism.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:29.770
What suspicion?

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:31.150
You know...

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.230
You've been recognized as a terrorist.

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:34.900
Wh-What's up with that?

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.450
Come on now, don't resist.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.610
Mr. Chikushi, what kind of joke—

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.450
It isn't.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.450
Okay Shindo, please take him.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.040
- Hey Chikuwa, what the hell is going on?
- Come on, let's go.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.660
- Hey, take this off.
- I'll listen to you later.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:52.250
<i>Mr. Shuta has been recognized as a terrorist?
KANAE System is truly running out of control.</i>

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:58.050
Mr. Chikushi, there's one item missing
from my belongings when I was hospitalized.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.680
You mean that CMD? I'm holding onto it.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.520
I had a feeling that would be the case.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.680
What will you do with it?

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.560
Quite a puzzling issue.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.360
What will we do with the KANAE System?

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:17.490
I think we should entrust it to a hero,
but what do you think?

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.070
That's not a bad idea.

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:22.160
Especially coming from you.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:23.330
Right?

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:26.580
KOKI SUIDO

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.580
Seventeen people were arrested
for suspicion of terrorism?

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.040
Is Hazard Cast bugging out?

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:38.340
With a riot going on in town, the KANAE System
has gone over capacity in terms of possibilities.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.930
The BRAIN is starting to lose its ability
of accurate decision-making.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:47.850
According to what you said, Gori doesn't know
that Asumi is in agony inside that thing, right?

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:49.350
Help me.

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:52.440
Then we should be shoving the truth
right into his face.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:57.150
How will you make someone
who has never seen a Vision believe all this?

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.280
Well, tell the truth as it—

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.950
He won't accept it.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:04.830
No, he just can't afford to accept it.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:11.920
If we can prove the existence of a conscience,
we might be able to convince Gori Suido.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:16.960
However, to do that,
we need the CMD that Sakiko retrieved.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:20.340
Though we have no idea where it is right now.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:24.760
I see. So it has disappeared at some point,
like I had thought.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.680
Okay, then please work
without overexerting yourself.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:35.310
<i>So Tsuzuragawa doesn't know
the whereabouts of that CMD either.</i>

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.190
<i>I can't save Asumi like this.</i>

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.700
- We got one over here now.
- Put it out!

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.990
Nothing can replace safety and security.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:49.200
- We can't even afford an unlikely event.
- It's too late if someone falls victim.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.460
It's information you can provide
if you're living a just life.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.460
Safety and security with the KANAE System!

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:56.170
ORDER AND STABILITY FOR THE TOWN!

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.380
If you can't synchronize with us,
get out of the 24th Ward!

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.380
Don't rob us of our safety!

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.170
Rotten apples should burn in hell!

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:06.140
<i>With all the protests
happening in Shantytown,</i>

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.140
Mrs. Kiriko.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:09.720
<i>Hazard Cast has shown a sudden increase
in its rate of criminal predictions.</i>

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.100
What is it, Mari?

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:13.310
My calls to Shu aren't going through.
Have you heard from him?

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:16.610
Actually, not at all.
He's not even answering my texts.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:19.980
I hope he's not doing
anything dangerous again.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:24.740
That reminds me. The Nanba Seika master got
asked to voluntarily head to the police station.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.490
Huh? Why?

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:29.950
Apparently Hazard Cast said
that he was a dangerous individual.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:33.210
The Nanba boy can't even kill an aphid.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:37.540
<i>Shu, where did you go at a time like this?</i>

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:37.000
A lot of weird things are happening, huh?

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:41.300
This is some kind of mistake
so let me go already.

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:43.720
There's no way I'd pull off terrorism.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:47.680
Yeah, yeah. I know that.
This is kind of like protecting you.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.260
You'd be in trouble
if anyone else caught you, right?

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:54.810
I don't believe
that you're a terrorist either, Little Hero.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.270
Damn you. Don't mock me.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.480
I'm not mocking you.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.280
You saved Satchan.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.650
Take pride in how you're bad at giving up.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.700
Take pride? I'm not doing things
with that as my objective.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.410
Then what is your objective?

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:12.120
That's... not set...

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:17.500
When someone in front of you is in pain,
you feel like you should rescue them, right?

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.170
You don't want to give up on anything, right?

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.000
Isn't it impossible to save everything?

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:26.760
It's impossible for a human to save everything.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.930
To me, you sound like
you're escaping from reality.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.310
It's almost like an illness.

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:36.140
Or is there some sort of reason
for you to keep acting like that?

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.150
What are you talking about? I don't get it.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:41.020
TAKARA ELEMENTARY SCHOOL FIRE
INVESTIGATION REPORT 1

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.570
This is...

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:46.030
The investigation report
for the Takara Elementary School Fire.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:51.780
From one year ago, ever since this incident,
you stopped your activities as a hero.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.580
It was announced as an arson case,

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:58.040
but you, someone directly involved,
showed no signs of going after the culprit.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:02.630
If you were an ideal hero,
you would make sure to catch the arsonist.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:08.590
And I just wasn't convinced from that,
so I looked over all the reports from back then.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.100
Bingo.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:15.850
The fire department's report said the cause
of the Takara Elementary School Fire was...

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.600
a short circuit.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:27.530
Wow, this is great!
This is the Kizuna Train, right?

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:31.740
Yup, that's right. It'll be running
in the 24th Ward starting next year.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:33.990
Oh, you know a lot.

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:37.040
When I grow up,
I'm gonna be a train conductor.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.120
You like trains, huh?

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:42.540
All right, then why don't we draw
a huge picture of the Kizuna Train?

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:43.290
Okay.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.090
Oh, is that me?

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.300
Yup. That's you, Big Sister Kozue.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.590
What I want to be in the future...

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.640
Thank you, future conductor.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:53.470
Asumi, do you have something
you want to do in the future?

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.800
Mikiya, I want to ride it, too.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:54.600
Me?

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:56.430
Okay. I'll draw you on this train car over here.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:56.930
Let's see.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.890
Hurray. Is yellow okay?

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.890
I want to be like my mom.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.730
Like Mrs. Kanae?

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:06.570
Yeah. I want to do all sorts of things
for everyone in the 24th Ward.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.030
You're already doing that.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:09.900
No, not at all.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.910
How can I do it?

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:18.000
Maybe find someone who understands me,
just like my mom did?

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.790
Hey, Shuta.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:25.090
Do you like anyone?

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:29.010
Huh? I-I... Well, um...

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.130
I-Is it Mari?

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.760
Idiot, it's not like that with her.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.430
- Really?
- Yes, really!

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:44.190
Uh, I'm gonna go to the bathroom.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.230
Shuta?

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:51.740
I mean, Mari is just a childhood friend.

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:56.450
It's not like that.
And why, of all people, did Asumi...

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.500
Rats?

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:04.920
What's wrong?

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:05.960
Mari.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.050
Huh? Where's Asumi?

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:11.300
A-Asumi is watching the kids in the classroom.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.510
Oh, okay.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:18.310
Oh, that's right.
Ran and Koki brought a generator for us.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.560
Shu, can you help carry it?

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:21.890
Oh, sure.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:27.900
- Hey, Shuta.
- Hurry, hurry!

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.570
Yeah, I'm coming.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:38.620
That time, if I didn't let those rats go...

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.120
Shuta.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:40.790
Asumi wouldn't have...

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:40.120
Shuta...

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.290
Shuta!

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:44.120
Oh... I...

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:45.960
Shuta, are you all right?

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.590
The Takara Elementary School Fire
was caused by a short circuit.

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:59.560
But Gori Suido wanted the public opinion
to support the KANAE System,

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:01.390
so he fabricated an arsonist.

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.930
And he's using Asumi,

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:07.270
who passed away from the incident,
for the sake of safety in the 24th Ward.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:09.190
You know about Asumi?

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:12.940
I'm an alum of the Kasuga Lab,
just like Kanae.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:15.990
Why do you think
I joined SARG in the first place?

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:20.700
I have a vague idea
of what you guys are trying to do right now.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:23.370
Give me your hand.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:26.750
What's this?

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:28.170
You heard from Satchan, right?

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:34.130
It's a CMD with the KANAE System's mapping data
that she retrieved from the Cornucopia.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:40.350
If you hand this to Ran and prove, then disclose,
the existence of Asumi's conscience,

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:42.810
the KANAE System will come to a halt.

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:47.390
If you hand this to Koki,
and run the program that Satchan provided,

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:51.400
Asumi will remain dormant
within the KANAE System forever.

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:56.030
Who to hand it to? Shuta, you decide that.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:00.700
How will you settle your past?

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:06.910
I don't get it.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:14.920
I don't get any of it!

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.380
<i>Kill Asumi?</i>

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:19.640
<i>Put her to sleep?</i>

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:22.510
<i>Everyone is thinking so selfishly.</i>

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:26.890
<i>It's strange, right? Why does Asumi
have to go through so much agony?</i>

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:28.980
<i>She already died once.</i>

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:32.190
<i>Why does Asumi
have to go through such horrible things?</i>

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:33.690
<i>Asumi's not alive?</i>

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:35.150
<i>Just a residual conscience?</i>

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:36.900
<i>Of course not.</i>

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.660
<i>Asumi is still in the 24th Ward.</i>

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.870
<i>She can eat the Golden Sunrise that I baked.</i>

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:45.330
<i>She can draw huge art with Ran.</i>

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.790
<i>She can do volunteer work with Koki.</i>

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:51.710
<i>She could've done lots of stuff like that.
She would've wanted to.</i>

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:55.050
<i>But now I have to choose her future?</i>

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:57.300
<i>That's... That's....</i>

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:02.300
I can't choose something like that!

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:06.970
AOI BAKERY

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:06.970
ITADAKI

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:08.680
Welcome back.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:13.310
Mrs. Kiriko, he's back.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:14.520
Shuta!

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:16.480
Oh. I-I'm home.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.780
Where were you in a time like this?

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.110
On a stroll...

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.110
What if something happened to you?

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:24.950
Well, we're glad he came back safe and sound.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.700
If you say so, Mari.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.080
Shu.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:33.380
This is good timing.
Help out with the morning batch right now.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:31.710
Looks like something happened.

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.050
So?

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:38.340
It's really hard to explain.

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:42.970
Here I was worried
and sitting under the cold skies all night.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:44.720
I-I feel bad about that.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.140
Then explain.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:50.940
I heard from Ms. Tsuzuragawa.

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:55.230
So just Asumi's conscience remains?

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:58.780
This is too sci-fi so it's not really sinking in.

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:02.700
But I do understand
that Asumi still exists in this world.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:08.040
I don't get it well either,
but it made me a little happy.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:13.120
Suddenly I'm being told
that I need to erase or don't erase...

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:18.050
Shu, you think that it was your fault
Asumi died, right?

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:19.840
What are you saying?

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:23.880
I'm sorry, Shu. I actually did notice it.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:27.350
That you felt responsible for the fire.

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:32.350
That day, I noticed as well, but I left it alone.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.020
Yeah, I coming.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:37.940
Huh? Is something there?

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:40.070
Mari, can you help us out?

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:41.610
Oh, okay.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:43.950
I've been regretting it ever since.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.320
It's the same with me.

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:51.200
If we had gotten rid of those rats,
that fire wouldn't have happened.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:54.080
Mari, you...

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:59.170
Shu, you should talk it out with Asumi.

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:00.300
With Asumi?

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:06.550
Yeah. Take all of the feelings you have pent up,
and tell them to her.

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:10.100
But, I...

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:11.560
What?

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.100
I'm scared.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.980
I'm scared of meeting Asumi.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:20.020
It's all right.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:23.740
I'm sure Asumi will be forgiving.

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:26.160
I mean, we're talking about Asumi.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:29.620
I can't imagine her
harboring a grudge against someone.

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:34.790
The person who won't forgive you... is you.

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:39.080
Shu, you're a bit awkward.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:42.420
So you don't know
how to get along with your emotions.

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.510
That means you just have to act it out, right?

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:47.050
Mari.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:53.520
I want to contact Ran and Koki,
but I can't get a hold of either of them.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:57.440
Oh, boys are so troublesome.

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:02.400
Yup. Okay. Then write them letters.
I'll go deliver them.

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.740
But I don't even know where they are.

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:07.280
Besides, we can't spend
too much time on this, either.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.370
It's fine. Leave this to me.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:19.000
Let's bomb Gori Suido with our anger!

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.800
That's quite an influence you got.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:30.590
Overloading the future predictions
of the KANAE System with this demo

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:31.890
to force it out of control.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.020
That's the future you painted, right?

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.640
Are you dissatisfied
with how my work turned out?

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.190
The scale is getting bigger and bigger.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:42.940
At this rate,
we won't simply end with injured people.

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:44.360
Are you still going to do it?

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:47.990
What's this?

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:51.780
This contains Di-VA's development data
that Kunai left behind.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:55.620
I heard that his PC and peripherals
were all seized as evidence.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:15:00.540
This was mailed to me.
I received it after Kunai passed.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:04.090
It was perhaps his act of atonement.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.630
Hold on to it as a good luck charm.

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:12.510
Is this the right thing to do, Kunai?

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:14.260
Ran.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:16.180
This is from Mari.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:18.480
That's from Shu's place.

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:23.400
Damn it. At this rate, I won't make it in time.

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:24.820
Mr. Koki.

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:29.900
Damn it. SARG is immobilized
from peacekeeping. Who else?

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:28.280
I have just returned. I will take over now.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:32.450
At this rate, I won't be able to save Asumi.

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:34.490
I can't save the KANAE System, either.

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:37.200
What should I do? What can I do?

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:41.870
Tsuzuragawa?

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:44.420
She slapped him.

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:45.460
She slapped him hard.

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:47.550
Get a grip on yourself.

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:49.800
Tsuzuragawa.

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:54.510
Mr. Koki, you are the son
of Lady Kanae who I admire so much.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:58.020
I've watched you grow
this whole time, right by your side.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:00.350
That's why I can tell

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:04.520
that you're someone who can definitely
guide us to the correct future.

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:06.360
What's this?

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:09.280
I've been asked by Ms. Mari Sakuragi
to give this to you.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:11.280
Apparently it's from Mr. Shuta.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:12.780
From Shuta?

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:16.780
This is...

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.790
I have the data
Carneades recovered.
I'll be waiting
at Takara Elementary.
Shuta

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.670
Sheesh, Shu.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:28.420
I'll leave this place to you.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.260
Yes.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:31.300
Take care on your way.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.300
Yeah.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:47.570
I'm here, Shu.

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:51.240
Shuta. Is it true that you have the CMD?

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.400
This thing, right?

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.780
That's it. We can save Asumi
from her agony with it.

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:59.700
Stop. The right answer
is to use it to stop the KANAE System.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.660
Ran, do you now what you're saying?

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:05.960
Same for you, Ko.
You want to sacrifice Asumin to create safety?

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:08.590
That's enough.
Shuta, hurry up and hand it over.

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:10.380
No, it's mine.

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:13.510
Shuta. Are you mocking us?

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:16.010
You called us out here. What do you want?

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:19.390
I don't know.

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.640
I don't know.

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:28.560
I don't know what the right answer is,
what I should choose, or what I want to do...

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:30.400
I don't know at all.

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:34.650
Ouch! What was that for?

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:36.530
Just stay there forever.

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.620
I'm going to move forward.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:42.240
No matter what sacrifices I have to make,
I can't afford to stand still right here.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:45.080
Like I'd let you.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:49.080
A future built upon someone's sacrifice
is not progress.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:50.960
I'll break down everything like that.

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:53.090
That's the future we should choose.

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:54.970
Are you seriously braced for that?

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:56.840
What are you...

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:58.970
Aren't you guys hesitating as well?

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:03.020
Aren't you closing away your emotions because
you want Asumi to become a thing of the past?

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:04.020
Of course not—

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:06.350
That's how I was.

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:13.030
I had a vague idea that the fire on that day
was caused by a cord the rats bit through.

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:17.280
I knew I was the one who killed Asumi.

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:20.530
But when Asumi called me,

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:24.620
I put a lid on all that and made myself believe
that she was still alive.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:27.040
Because if I didn't...

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:31.460
I felt like the connection with Asumi
that I finally found would go away.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:35.970
I felt like Asumi would really be gone, and so...

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:39.840
I don't know what would be good for Asumi.

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:43.180
You're still acting spoiled after all this time!

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:44.600
She...

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:47.390
She wished for everyone's happiness
more than anyone else.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:52.400
She inherited Mom's wishes, and should feel
that she needs to protect our town.

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:55.820
So at the least,
we can use that CMD to free her from—

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:56.650
Objection!

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.410
Ran, you've been nothing but—

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:01.200
And that's your ego, Ko.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:03.700
Asumin is in agony from her nightmares.

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:06.620
The errors in Hazard Cast
proves that more than anything else.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:10.040
Then the best thing to do
would be to destroy the entire system.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.040
Who decided that?

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:15.670
We selfishly trapped Asumi inside that system.

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:17.090
You muscle-brain.

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:17.880
We forced predictions of the future on her.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:20.470
And now we're talking about
how she should sleep or be destroyed.

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:22.600
Isn't that being too selfish?

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:24.510
Why can't you grow up already?

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:27.680
I don't want to be someone like that!

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:29.390
That can be said for anyone.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:32.440
We all get older.

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:35.980
We grow, we fall in love, we have families,

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:37.820
and we die!

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:42.410
Yeah, that's right. That's it.

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.990
If Asumi was still alive, I'm sure she—

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:45.870
Shut up!

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:48.250
Shut up, shut up, shut up, shut up!

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.870
I'm Asumi's older brother.

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:53.630
When I wake up in the morning,
when I'm eating meals, when I go home...

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:57.380
She's not there.
She's gone. She's just not there.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:02.220
Don't act like you're the only victim.
You took Kunai's life!

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:04.220
Do you understand that?

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:08.180
I understand that more than anyone.

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:10.730
I didn't want to kill him at all.

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:12.690
I... I...

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:14.650
I never wanted to do something like that.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:19.070
For my ideals, I even abandoned Tsuzuragawa.

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:21.530
Are you in agony?

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:25.370
That's really your ego speaking.
Don't force self-sacrifice upon others!

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:26.120
Shut up, graffiti boy!

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:29.620
And what about you?
You're still doing everything that 0th tells you.

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:33.620
You claim everything is for the weak,
but you're putting their lives in danger!

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:36.090
Little ol' me ain't satisfied with all this.

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:38.670
Now is not the time
to worry about the means...

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:39.760
I knew it!

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:43.130
You're hesitating!

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:44.800
You're being stubborn!

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:47.510
If you have something to say, say it!

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:49.770
Then let me say this.

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:52.270
Workout idiots shouldn't get carried away.

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:57.480
Who's the one who kept running
from Asumi forever and got buff because of it?

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:00.900
Like really, you're one to talk!

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:04.660
Just how long are you going to mope?
It irritates me to watch you.

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:07.320
Why don't you do that hero thing
or whatever it was?

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:08.950
But that was for Asumi.

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:14.750
I became Mr. 24 for Asumi's sake.

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:17.670
It's meaningless if she's not here.

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:24.130
Asumi. Asumi, why aren't you here?

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:25.800
That's my line.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:28.930
I want to see Asumi.
I want to see her and talk to her.

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:34.020
I want to see her, too. I'll show her
my brand new art piece if I can see her.

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:36.560
I'll let her eat my Golden Sunrise.

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:41.570
The Golden Sunrise
that proves I became a qualified baker.

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:54.620
Damn it. I wanna see her!

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:57.040
I want to see her more!

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:59.920
I'm the one who wants to see her most!

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:21.070
Hey, can't we see Asumi?

00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:23.820
See her, you say?

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:26.990
I can't decide like this.

00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:33.160
I want to meet Asumi, talk to her,
listen to how she feels, and tell her my feelings.

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:36.330
I think I can finally move on
when that happens.

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:38.540
That's impossible, Shu.

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:42.000
There's no way we can contact her
from this side.

00:22:42.460 --> 00:22:45.630
If all three of us are together,
nothing is impossible.

00:22:48.680 --> 00:22:51.140
Please, lend me a hand.

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:54.520
Meeting a conscience
that wanders the digital world...

00:22:54.680 --> 00:22:57.270
Unless you digitized yourself...

00:22:59.730 --> 00:23:01.940
Maybe fate really exists.

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:03.190
What's that?

00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:05.990
I was able to get my hands on Di-VA's data.

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:09.490
The Cipher was based
on the same technology, right?

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:11.700
So if we have ample calculation resources...

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:16.290
I see. The KANAE System utilizes cPhones
from all over the 24th Ward

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:18.790
to perform calculations
by dispersed computing.

00:23:18.790 --> 00:23:20.420
With my administrative authorization...

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:21.670
Hey, what are you talking about?

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:24.040
A discussion to create a miracle.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:26.170
Can we see Asumi?

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:29.220
The conditions are tough, but the possibility...

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:30.550
...is not zero, right?

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:31.800
Well, yeah.

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:37.180
You can't, Shuta.

00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:40.440
I don't want to see you.

00:23:40.900 --> 00:23:42.940
I beg of you, please don't come here.

00:23:52.740 --> 00:23:53.570
This is...

00:23:53.740 --> 00:23:55.910
Sheesh, was she aiming for this?

00:23:55.910 --> 00:23:57.830
She might be watching.

00:23:57.830 --> 00:23:59.960
ASUMI

00:23:58.160 --> 00:23:59.410
- Asumi.
- Asumin.
